# Expression Language Reference

The expression language used by rules, computed fields, transforms and controls.

## Pages

| Page | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| [Syntax](./expression/syntax) | Lexical forms, operators, AST nodes and primitive methods |
| [Built-in Functions](./expression/functions) | Annotated callable functions |
| [Program Mode](./expression/program-mode) | use, let, return, when and runtime modules |
| [Examples](./expression/examples) | Hand-written end-to-end examples |
| [SQL Translation](./sql) | PostgreSQL and SurrealQL support |

## Quick facts

- **313 documented built-in functions**
- **Exact decimal arithmetic**: `0.1 + 0.2` is `0.3`.
- **A missing value is unknown**, as in R and SQL: see [Missing values](./expression/syntax#missing-values).
- **Currency literals** support common currency symbols.
- **Program mode** supports runtime modules and async evaluation.

